  "summary": "Five candidate documents directly apply federated learning (decentralised training without pooled records) or closely related methods to protein molecular function prediction. [V0153] (Adebayo et al., 2026) applies decentralised training without pooled records to the ProtMap dataset, achieving 0.79 AUROC. [V0154] (Brennan et al., 2018) applies the same federated approach to the FireScope dataset, reporting F1=0.86. [V0155] (Chen et al., 2019) uses decentralised training without pooled records on ChurnBench, achieving accuracy of 0.93. [V0156] (Duarte et al., 2020) applies decentralised training without pooled records to MetroFlow, reporting MAE of 0.65. [V0159] (Duarte et al., 2020) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles to ChurnBench for protein molecular function prediction, obtaining MAE 0.69. Documents such as [V0149] and [V0164] address protein function but do not use federated/decentralised methods; documents such as [V0107] and [V0083] use decentralised training but not for protein function. Documents that only mention federated learning for protein function as prior work (e.g., [V0109], [V0126], [V0192], [V0032], [V0003]) are excluded as non-applications.",
